WEBVTT

00:12.480 --> 00:15.490
For the great service she has 
performed for the imperial family,

00:15.990 --> 00:21.990
the Order of the Imperial Rose is 
hereby bestowed upon Lady Clorence.

00:26.940 --> 00:28.440
And...

00:32.240 --> 00:37.370
I, Minchester de Romanoff, in 
recognition of her great service,

00:37.370 --> 00:41.660
grant Elise de Clorence 
the noble rank of knight.

00:49.510 --> 00:51.540
It was a magnificent ceremony!

00:51.540 --> 00:55.240
Indeed! And to think, it's the first 
time it's been awarded to a woman!

00:55.240 --> 00:59.020
I should expect no less of the 
lady chosen by Prince Linden.

00:59.020 --> 01:00.410
I, um...

01:00.410 --> 01:02.970
I read about it in the newspaper.

01:02.970 --> 01:09.030
Before you become crown princess, you're 
doing volunteer work at a hospital, aren't you?

01:09.030 --> 01:12.790
No, my work as a doctor isn't 
simply volunteer work.

01:12.790 --> 01:16.290
And you're still so young! 
How very impressive.

01:16.290 --> 01:20.800
I just know you'll become 
a wise crown princess.

01:28.610 --> 01:30.310
<i>What do you think?</i>

01:30.720 --> 01:35.870
I'd like to put an end to our 
wager here. What about you?

01:38.270 --> 01:42.740
<i>If... If things keep on as they 
are and I lose the wager...</i>

01:44.130 --> 01:45.880
<i>No, I can't lose my nerve now!</i>

01:46.320 --> 01:48.830
<i>The physician's exam is in two days.</i>

01:49.620 --> 01:52.700
<i>I will become a doctor, 
no matter what it takes!</i>

03:33.860 --> 03:37.640
Allow me to say it once more. 
Congratulations, Lady Clorence.

03:37.640 --> 03:39.940
Thank you, Your Majesty.

03:39.940 --> 03:44.490
I'm astonished to receive 
such a prestigious award.

03:44.980 --> 03:50.230
What are you saying? Considering 
your actions, it's only natural.

03:50.640 --> 03:52.250
I'm honored.

03:53.390 --> 03:56.260
Today is such a good day.

03:56.810 --> 04:00.910
The sky is blue. The music is pleasant.

04:01.820 --> 04:05.770
The people's faces are 
overflowing with smiles.

04:06.740 --> 04:11.530
It would be nice if days like 
today could continue forever.

04:16.290 --> 04:18.910
Have I said something strange?

04:18.910 --> 04:21.020
No, it isn't that.

04:21.280 --> 04:22.580
It's just that...

04:22.580 --> 04:25.530
I think it's a lovely wish.

04:26.000 --> 04:28.650
We're free to wish what we like, aren't we?

04:28.910 --> 04:30.350
Yes, we are.

04:31.930 --> 04:36.540
I know that the reality is that 
there aren't only good days.

04:36.980 --> 04:41.300
<i>His Majesty's face seems pale to me.</i>

04:41.300 --> 04:45.110
<i>He is still being treated for his 
chronic illness, diabetes, but...</i>

04:45.800 --> 04:48.790
Were you able to sleep well last night?

04:49.800 --> 04:50.830
Yes.

04:50.830 --> 04:55.090
You don't have any symptoms like 
dizziness or sudden weakness?

04:55.090 --> 04:56.890
No, I don't.

04:56.890 --> 04:57.960
Then, is there something else—

04:57.960 --> 04:59.810
Lady Clorence.

05:00.170 --> 05:02.810
This isn't a hospital.

05:03.240 --> 05:04.440
Besides...

05:05.600 --> 05:08.340
you are today's main event.

05:10.760 --> 05:15.720
Look. There is someone over there 
who wishes to speak with you.

05:15.720 --> 05:17.070
Go on over there.

05:20.910 --> 05:22.020
Juliane.

05:22.950 --> 05:24.380
All right.

05:24.380 --> 05:29.850
But if you start feeling ill, please 
tell someone as soon as possible.

05:29.850 --> 05:30.930
I will.

05:30.930 --> 05:32.590
Then, if you will excuse me.

05:38.620 --> 05:39.580
Your Majesty.

05:40.370 --> 05:42.260
Crown Prince Linden.

05:42.260 --> 05:45.110
Father, I've brought another 
glass if you'd like.

05:45.110 --> 05:48.860
Oh, thank you, Linden. I think I will.

05:58.580 --> 06:01.370
You shouldn't drink it 
all at once like that.

06:01.370 --> 06:04.750
It doesn't matter. Today is a good day.

06:04.750 --> 06:06.520
Now, one more glass.

06:15.750 --> 06:16.510
Your Majesty?

06:16.780 --> 06:19.020
M-My chest...

06:24.500 --> 06:25.530
Father!

06:28.260 --> 06:30.120
Father! Father!

06:30.120 --> 06:30.940
Your Majesty...

06:31.280 --> 06:33.930
Hurry! Call Viscount Ven here!

06:34.870 --> 06:36.110
Your Majesty!

06:39.590 --> 06:41.250
<i>There isn't a pulse.</i>

06:41.250 --> 06:44.580
<i>He hasn't simply fainted. 
This is a heart attack!</i>

06:44.580 --> 06:46.060
What's happened?

06:47.190 --> 06:48.640
He's had a heart attack!

06:49.370 --> 06:54.190
Viscount Ven, please begin administering 
His Majesty a cardiotonic agent right away!

06:54.190 --> 06:56.040
Continue at four minute intervals!

06:56.040 --> 06:56.770
All right.

07:02.210 --> 07:04.460
<i>Please, Your Majesty...</i>

07:04.460 --> 07:06.790
<i>Come back! Please!</i>

07:14.660 --> 07:16.280
His pulse is back!

07:18.280 --> 07:19.640
I'm so glad.

07:19.640 --> 07:20.790
Oh, Your Majesty...

07:21.360 --> 07:25.500
His heart attack has only just happened, 
so we can't rest easy just yet.

07:25.500 --> 07:28.180
Please continue to monitor 
his condition closely.

07:28.180 --> 07:28.910
Yes, miss.

07:29.250 --> 07:34.470
Systolic blood pressure, 70. 
Pulse rate, 40. Breaths, 20.

07:35.600 --> 07:37.690
<i>Is he in severe shock?</i>

07:37.690 --> 07:40.250
Take him to Imperial Cross Hospital!

07:40.250 --> 07:41.060
Yes, sir!

07:44.810 --> 07:47.540
Continue to monitor his pulse on the way.

07:47.540 --> 07:50.700
If his pulse rate should drop, 
please say something right away.

07:50.700 --> 07:51.960
Understood.

07:52.250 --> 07:54.750
This has become rather dire.

07:54.750 --> 07:56.480
They said it was a heart attack.

07:56.480 --> 07:58.260
Will he be able to recover?

07:59.450 --> 08:02.130
More importantly, why did 
it happen so suddenly?

08:02.130 --> 08:03.990
Did his chronic illness suddenly worsen?

08:03.990 --> 08:07.150
Or could there have been poison in his wine?

08:18.760 --> 08:23.080
My sincerest apologies, but the 
situation does seem suspicious.

08:23.080 --> 08:25.740
Will you come with us, please?

08:26.520 --> 08:27.540
Yes.

08:42.490 --> 08:45.330
<i>If we don't alleviate his 
state of shock quickly,</i>

08:45.330 --> 08:47.430
<i>it will cause negative aftereffects.</i>

08:49.750 --> 08:50.930
<i>Your Majesty...</i>

08:58.560 --> 09:01.750
<i>I don't ever want to feel like that again.</i>

09:02.710 --> 09:05.600
Please make sure he's getting 
enough transfusions.

09:05.600 --> 09:10.280
And if his blood pressure drops or there's 
any change in his state of consciousness,

09:10.280 --> 09:12.240
please contact me right away.

09:12.240 --> 09:13.320
Yes, miss.

09:15.460 --> 09:17.960
<i>He didn't look like he was feeling well,</i>

09:17.960 --> 09:22.020
<i>but diabetes isn't the sort of disease 
that causes a sudden heart attack.</i>

09:23.640 --> 09:26.140
<i>What could have caused this?</i>

09:37.010 --> 09:39.760
Regarding the failed attempt 
to poison His Majesty...

09:40.750 --> 09:44.420
Poison, you say? How can you say 
that when there's no proof?

09:45.690 --> 09:48.940
You're saying that it wasn't 
an attempted poisoning?

09:49.240 --> 09:50.430
Of course it wasn't.

09:50.430 --> 09:55.280
Then why did he spit up blood and collapse 
right after drinking a celebratory cup?

09:55.280 --> 09:57.190
Because of his chronic illness.

09:57.500 --> 10:02.390
His Majesty's illness isn't one which would 
cause him to clutch his chest and cough up blood.

10:02.390 --> 10:06.280
And yet, immediately after drinking the 
cup Crown Prince Linden handed him,

10:06.280 --> 10:08.750
he collapsed in that manner.

10:08.750 --> 10:13.200
It's only natural to think
 it was poison, isn't it?

10:15.040 --> 10:20.180
Lady Clorence said that, based on the 
symptoms, it was unlikely to be poison.

10:20.180 --> 10:22.230
She is an outstanding doctor.

10:22.230 --> 10:24.980
We can trust her words above all else.

10:25.990 --> 10:28.380
How can we trust her words?

10:28.380 --> 10:33.330
She is Crown Prince Linden's fiancée and 
a daughter of the House of Clorence.

10:33.330 --> 10:36.480
It's certain that her findings are 
affected by her own self-interest.

10:38.200 --> 10:40.500
And she isn't a doctor yet.

10:40.500 --> 10:41.990
She's just an apprentice, isn't she?

10:42.270 --> 10:47.010
She lacks the objectivity necessary 
for a precise diagnosis.

10:47.010 --> 10:51.360
But there isn't any evidence that there 
was poison in the wine, is there?

10:51.360 --> 10:55.250
His Majesty's current 
condition is the proof.

10:55.560 --> 10:59.820
His Majesty, Emperor of the 
Great Britia Empire, has collapsed.

10:59.820 --> 11:04.890
And you mean to judge this tremendous 
incident simply on the visible circumstances?

11:04.890 --> 11:07.780
Is that how the House of Child does things?

11:12.060 --> 11:17.420
<i>At this rate, the crown prince really will 
lose his standing for murdering his father.</i>

11:17.420 --> 11:19.650
<i>I can't back down here.</i>

11:20.020 --> 11:24.260
According to the law of the empire, 
charges of murder and attempted murder

11:24.260 --> 11:27.660
cannot be pursued based on 
circumstantial evidence alone!

11:28.010 --> 11:33.040
If the crown prince is to be accused of 
a crime, there must be clear evidence!

11:33.040 --> 11:34.010
Nonetheless...

11:34.010 --> 11:35.420
That's enough.

11:36.370 --> 11:37.860
Marquis Ell,

11:37.860 --> 11:42.420
who holds the ultimate judicial 
power in this nation?

11:43.860 --> 11:45.670
His Majesty, the emperor.

11:45.670 --> 11:51.440
Then, with my father unconscious and my 
older brother in custody, who holds it now?

11:53.160 --> 11:54.930
You, Prince Mikhail.

11:55.320 --> 11:56.580
That's right.

11:56.580 --> 11:59.650
With regards to this attempted poisoning,

11:59.650 --> 12:02.630
passing judgment here and now is difficult.

12:02.630 --> 12:06.690
As all of you have said, there 
isn't clear evidence either way.

12:10.040 --> 12:14.960
However, if no other cause comes 
to light during treatment,

12:14.960 --> 12:17.700
my older brother will be 
accused of this crime.

12:31.350 --> 12:32.730
What did you want to discuss?

12:33.110 --> 12:36.980
Could this incident have been 
your doing, Marquis Amsel?

12:37.970 --> 12:42.240
The situation has continued 
to be unfavorable for us.

12:42.240 --> 12:46.840
I can't say that I never 
once thought about it,

12:46.840 --> 12:48.000
but it wasn't me.

12:49.960 --> 12:53.790
I do not know what caused 
His Majesty's heart attack.

12:53.790 --> 12:57.160
However, he has been stricken 
with illness for some time now.

12:57.160 --> 12:59.750
There's very little reason to 
anticipate his recovery, is there?

12:59.750 --> 13:04.390
Then, you're saying it's possible His Majesty 
may pass as soon as tomorrow?

13:05.700 --> 13:09.980
In order for Crown Prince Linden 
to prove his innocence,

13:09.980 --> 13:13.530
it will be necessary to show a 
clear cause for the heart attack.

13:13.530 --> 13:15.150
Regarding that,

13:15.150 --> 13:19.260
isn't it bad for us to allow Lady 
Clorence to treat His Majesty?

13:19.550 --> 13:20.880
It isn't an issue.

13:20.880 --> 13:27.450
Even for her, finding the cause of a sudden 
heart attack won't be easily done.

13:27.450 --> 13:28.420
However...

13:28.730 --> 13:30.590
this is a good opportunity.

13:30.590 --> 13:33.410
We will use it to force the 
crown prince from his position!

13:35.380 --> 13:39.240
I've already arranged for a 
newspaper to publish an article.

13:39.240 --> 13:42.160
Now we need only spread 
rumors among the commoners

13:42.160 --> 13:45.920
that Crown Prince Linden 
poisoned the emperor.

13:46.420 --> 13:48.990
Gossip is a terrifying thing.

13:48.990 --> 13:50.670
Even without definite proof,

13:50.670 --> 13:55.350
rumors beget more rumors, and they 
begin to feel like the truth.

13:56.180 --> 13:59.940
We will bring public opinion to our side. 
Is that what you mean?

14:00.280 --> 14:02.880
You will be contacted later. Wait for it.

14:05.530 --> 14:10.290
"Wait for it"? This is not 
the time to move slowly.

14:10.290 --> 14:12.880
That gentleman has a certain 
blitheness to him.

14:12.880 --> 14:15.390
He does. We, however...

14:15.390 --> 14:19.640
If it's for the greater cause, 
some sacrifices are unavoidable.

14:30.250 --> 14:33.010
That meeting was absolutely preposterous.

14:33.010 --> 14:35.130
The whole thing was clearly planned.

14:35.470 --> 14:38.290
His Highness, assassinate His Majesty?

14:38.290 --> 14:40.970
The nobles' faction suggested 
that with no grounds at all!

14:40.970 --> 14:45.010
Prince Linden has no reason
 to kill His Majesty.

14:45.010 --> 14:47.470
Where is Prince Linden now?

14:47.770 --> 14:50.000
He's been placed in the Hundreds House.

14:50.750 --> 14:52.490
So, he's being treated as a criminal.

14:52.810 --> 14:55.690
If no cause other than poison is discovered,

14:55.690 --> 14:58.130
there will be no means of stopping 
the noble faction's scheme.

14:58.130 --> 15:01.260
But there isn't a single thing we can do.

15:01.580 --> 15:06.920
Is praying for Lady Clorence to create 
a miracle all that's left to us?

15:09.400 --> 15:10.690
<i>Elise...</i>

15:18.010 --> 15:21.710
Systolic pressure, 85. 
Diastolic pressure, 40.

15:21.710 --> 15:25.030
It's gotten a little better, 
but it's still low.

15:25.030 --> 15:28.060
Yes. He should be receiving 
adequate infusions.

15:29.770 --> 15:32.230
<i>What could be causing this?</i>

15:35.440 --> 15:38.780
<i>Not many illnesses can 
cause shock like this.</i>

15:39.250 --> 15:41.960
<i>It should be among those I know of.</i>

15:42.960 --> 15:48.400
<i>I considered the idea that the noble faction 
was framing Prince Linden by using poison,</i>

15:49.260 --> 15:52.530
<i>but Mil would never use such craven methods.</i>

15:52.530 --> 15:53.810
<i>Besides which...</i>

15:54.350 --> 15:58.550
<i>there have been no changes in his body 
which would clearly point to poison.</i>

15:59.850 --> 16:02.430
<i>And in the examination of his 
heart and x-rays of his lungs...</i>

16:02.430 --> 16:04.480
<i>I didn't see any abnormalities.</i>

16:09.330 --> 16:12.240
<i>This isn't a matter of simply 
lacking technical ability.</i>

16:12.240 --> 16:14.140
<i>I must be overlooking something!</i>

16:14.140 --> 16:16.220
<i>What could it be?</i>

16:16.220 --> 16:18.130
We can't continue like this.

16:18.130 --> 16:21.990
Y-Yes, you're right! We should 
conduct a different examination!

16:21.990 --> 16:25.510
No, I mean you, Rose.

16:26.780 --> 16:28.580
Me?

16:28.580 --> 16:30.510
You haven't slept a wink since yesterday.

16:30.510 --> 16:32.480
You haven't eaten much either, have you?

16:32.480 --> 16:33.930
Th-That's right.

16:33.930 --> 16:35.800
But I'm all right!

16:35.800 --> 16:37.380
Right now, every moment counts!

16:37.690 --> 16:41.860
Until now, even when your 
passion burned hottest,

16:41.860 --> 16:44.960
you always made logical, calm decisions,

16:44.960 --> 16:47.150
and provided accurate, 
appropriate treatments.

16:47.460 --> 16:49.230
But right now, you're different.

16:49.790 --> 16:52.030
You're not maintaining your own health.

16:52.030 --> 16:54.380
Do you think that, in that panicked state,

16:54.380 --> 16:56.530
you can truly see your patient clearly?

16:59.430 --> 17:02.660
Fortunately, His Majesty 
is stable at the moment.

17:03.020 --> 17:06.540
I'm here, and so is Viscount Ven.

17:06.540 --> 17:09.950
As long as there are no major changes, 
we are more than capable of handling this.

17:11.580 --> 17:14.730
Why don't you go out and 
breathe a little fresh air?

17:23.950 --> 17:25.860
<i>How pathetic.</i>

17:27.030 --> 17:31.940
<i>I declared so arrogantly that I'd 
become a doctor no matter what,</i>

17:32.620 --> 17:36.840
<i>but I can't even figure out how to save 
the life of someone so dear to me.</i>

17:39.350 --> 17:40.710
There's an extra edition!

17:42.710 --> 17:45.710
Extra! Extra, extra!

17:46.470 --> 17:47.810
Extra!

17:50.720 --> 17:53.340
"A planned heart attack"?

17:53.340 --> 17:56.970
"The mastermind behind the assassination... 
was Crown Prince Linden"?

17:56.970 --> 17:58.470
Is this true?

17:58.470 --> 18:00.770
His Highness, the crown prince, wouldn't...

18:00.770 --> 18:04.980
No, it's possible. Maybe he wanted 
to make the empire his own!

18:04.980 --> 18:09.470
And I heard that he's being held 
in the Hundreds House right now.

18:27.950 --> 18:29.160
<i>Father...</i>

18:30.830 --> 18:33.060
Your Highness, if you'll permit me,

18:33.060 --> 18:35.070
Lady Clorence is here.

18:47.680 --> 18:49.980
<i>He looks a little gaunt.</i>

18:49.980 --> 18:51.020
Come over here.

18:54.980 --> 18:57.150
How is my father's condition?

18:58.750 --> 19:01.410
It still isn't very good.

19:01.840 --> 19:03.020
I see.

19:08.680 --> 19:12.930
I know that all of you are 
doing everything you can.

19:13.700 --> 19:14.820
Your Highness...

19:17.000 --> 19:18.420
Pathetic, isn't it?

19:18.420 --> 19:19.400
What?

19:20.650 --> 19:23.980
I have absolutely no power.

19:26.690 --> 19:27.960
I didn't back then...

19:31.120 --> 19:32.350
and I don't now.

19:34.740 --> 19:38.550
Not being able to do a single 
thing... It's just pathetic.

19:52.230 --> 19:53.360
Your Highness.

19:54.360 --> 19:55.710
It's all right.

19:56.800 --> 20:00.670
His Majesty will get better! 
I'll make sure of that!

20:01.170 --> 20:02.350
Elise...

20:17.100 --> 20:20.780
I'll do it again. I'll look into 
each possible cause one at a time.

20:21.320 --> 20:23.660
Please wait, Lady Clorence!

20:24.460 --> 20:26.810
We've just had a report.

20:26.810 --> 20:29.710
His Majesty... His Majesty has 
fallen into severe shock again!

20:30.010 --> 20:31.080
What?

20:31.080 --> 20:34.560
We'll call a carriage for you immediately! 
Please wait just a moment!

20:34.560 --> 20:36.090
O-Of course!

20:38.290 --> 20:39.440
<i>Your Majesty...</i>

20:40.610 --> 20:43.600
Lady Elise de Clorence?

20:49.750 --> 20:52.090
<i>They're from the nobles' faction.</i>

20:55.350 --> 20:58.880
We cannot allow you to go to His Majesty!

20:59.730 --> 21:01.610
You'll die here!

21:09.670 --> 21:10.780
After her!

21:15.870 --> 21:17.490
We can't let her get away!

21:18.080 --> 21:21.500
<i>I can't let them find me. If they do, then...</i>

21:22.170 --> 21:27.810
<i>then why did I begin living 
this life as Elise again?</i>

21:28.920 --> 21:31.940
<i>At the very least, I have 
to save His Majesty.</i>

21:35.020 --> 21:37.690
<i>I absolutely can't die here!</i>

21:40.280 --> 21:42.550
Where are that lot we hired?

21:42.550 --> 21:44.190
They're on their way here now!

22:06.220 --> 22:09.970
A Wish
